sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0248 Cluster router resolver amendment; one shared member policy for peer reconcile, converge and Cluster lifecycle.
  %% Tightened: flow-tighten rules 6, 22, 27, 28: persistence, live apply and check form one Ansible phase.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: none · managed DNS policy changes
  %% kind: fleet.peer_dns
  autonumber
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Target Node<br/>reached over ssh
  Note over GW: Render changed policy<br/>Cluster and VPN scopes
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - an active, managed Linux Node with an active Cluster membership, LAN address and systemd-resolved delegate support selects its Cluster's ready LAN Router, including the Router itself
  %%> - all other managed peers keep the VPN split policy; a conflicting explicit DNS override refuses before mutation
  %%> - a roleless member needs managed SSH enrollment, not a workload role; unmanaged devices are reported without claiming convergence
  %%> Result:
  %%> - a complete per-Node projection, revision and digest, including delegate capability and the public resolver invariant
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-fleet-peer-dns
  %%> Inputs:
  %%> - Cluster delegate with one LAN server, owned suffixes, remaining VPN domains, probes and pinned SSH connection; no global resolver replacement
  %%> - the same projection is passed to this phase by the shared DNS publication during a Cluster transition
  Note over SW: Write the intent
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - ships the playbook and private run file; a matching policy still gets its end check
  SW->>N: Apply member DNS policy<br/>Ansible phase
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - checks systemd-resolved delegate support and the LAN route; the vpn Node answers WireGuard addresses and the Router resolver answers its LAN members with LAN addresses
  %%> - snapshots owned policy, persists the Cluster-only delegate and remaining WireGuard hook and marker, applies both scopes, and checks them in the same phase
  %%> - leaves LAN-link DNS, addresses, routes, DHCP, resolv.conf and global resolved settings alone; reloads resolved only when the delegate file or live scope differs
  %%> Runtime failure:
  %%> - the delegate has no VPN server; Cluster DNS or LAN failure makes its Cluster lookups fail until repair, and Doctor reports it
  alt delegate support missing
    %% path: delegate-unsupported
    Note over N: Kept VPN DNS<br/>dns.cluster_delegate_unsupported
    %%> Result:
    %%> - systemd below 258 or missing delegate support removes any owned delegate; checks and records the complete VPN split policy as a successful degraded outcome
    %%> - Cluster lookups receive WireGuard answers and Doctor reports node.cluster_dns_delegate_unsupported; no second mechanism
  else delegate supported
    %% path: delegate-supported
    Note over N: Cluster delegate selected<br/>one LAN server · systemd 258+
    %%> Result:
    %%> - only Cluster domains use the delegate; LAN-link public DNS and remaining VPN domains keep their own scopes
  end
  alt effective policy matches
    %% path: succeeded
    N-->>SW: Policy checked<br/>revision · digest · scope
    %%> What it proves:
    %%> - on a supported member Cluster A uses LAN and AAAA is NODATA; unsupported members get WireGuard answers; other private and public names retain their selected resolvers
    %%> - on withdrawal the Cluster suffix uses VPN before the delegate is removed; no duplicate best-match domain remains
    %%> - an unchanged policy records a successful skip without a resolver reload
  else apply or check fails
    %% path: failed
    Note over N: Restore owned policy
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - restores captured persistent and live settings within the peer lock; leaves later revisions untouched
    %%> - failed recovery keeps its snapshot and reports dns.rollback_failed; the caller cannot retire the old Router
    N--xSW: Policy failed<br/>target · error_code
    %%> Retry:
    %%> - retain the failed target and repeat after repair; no workload or public DNS configuration is deleted
  end
  Note over SW: Remove the run folder
  %%> How:
  %%> - native completed dependencies wait for the phase, then remove disposable files on either outcome
  alt phase passed
    %% path: recorded
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal result
    %%> Result:
    %%> - records the applied policy; lifecycle callers can release their member cleanup barrier
  else phase failed
    %% path: refused
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>failed step · error_code
    %%> Result:
    %%> - records drift and retains the unfinished transition; no separate member queue owns a Cluster handover
  end
